								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=1446.msg21731#msg21731"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=1446.msg21731#msg21731">Re: New ignorant Stranger hip hop writer disses Blue Scholars - and no one cares</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #14 on:</b> March 21, 2007, 07:56:43 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">Ok now I&#039;m not gonna come in here swinging the massline flag because I&#039;m cool with a couple members however I would consider myself to be pretty unbiased as far as hip hop music is concerned... I mean I&#039;ve posted up links to Jim Jones/Young Jeezy/etc so it&#039;s not like I&#039;m so maladjusted backpacker who gets a screw face any time I hear Talib rock on a Midi Mafia or Neptunes joint... so with that said....<br /><br />Let&#039;s use a sports analogy.&nbsp; When the Yankees come into town, do they boo the guy on the .189 batting average?&nbsp; Nope, they boo Alex Rodriguez and Derek Jeter.&nbsp; Furthermore, saying the majority of CM/BS fans are white is 100% true... the same could be said for 50 Cent, D. Black, Dyme Def, and any rap act for that matter. 86% of hip hop consumers I&#039;ve heard are white, so if anything compared to that number there is a higher amount of minorities present at BS shows.&nbsp; I mean jesus how many people here have been to a Dead Prez show?&nbsp; The entire thing is white.<br /><br />As far as ignoring the gangster scene, no group coming out locally right now has more buzz than dyme def... Besides, you can&#039;t force people to listen to stuff.&nbsp; That&#039;s ignorant.&nbsp; As far as the local handshakes/daps thing, Ive been to about 4-5 local events in the last few months and a ML&#039;er has been there each time.&nbsp; So take that as you will.<br /><br />All in all though it&#039;s just an article but you can&#039;t fault certain people for being defensive of something they&#039;ve poured so much of themselves into.&nbsp; <br /><br /></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
